# DHCP Server Lab — Cisco Packet Tracer

## Objective
Configure a router as a DHCP server to automatically 
assign IP addresses to client PCs on a LAN.

## Topology
- 1x Cisco 2911 Router (DHCP Server)
- 1x Cisco 2960 Switch
- 3x PCs (DHCP Clients)

## IP Addressing Scheme
| Device  | IP Address      | Assignment |
|---------|----------------|------------|
| Router  | 192.168.1.1    | Static     |
| PC1     | 192.168.1.11   | DHCP       |
| PC2     | 192.168.1.12   | DHCP       |
| PC3     | 192.168.1.13   | DHCP       |

## DHCP Pool Configuration
- Network: 192.168.1.0/24
- Default Gateway: 192.168.1.1
- DNS Server: 8.8.8.8
- Excluded Range: 192.168.1.1 – 192.168.1.10

## Protocols Used
- DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol)

## What I Learned
- How DHCP automates IP address assignment
- How to configure a DHCP pool on a Cisco router
- How to exclude static addresses from the DHCP range
- How to verify clients received addresses using ipconfig

## Tools Used
- Cisco Packet Tracer 8.x
